Aurora model fetcher

Run aurora-model-fetch rnnoise, aurora-model-fetch df3, or
aurora-model-fetch whisper-tiny.en. The command prints the verified local path.
Use --cache DIR to select a cache; use --refresh to replace corrupt cached data
only after a new download verifies. See aurora-model-fetch(1) for details.

Installation starts no service and downloads no weights. The installed
models.json records the immutable source, licence and SHA-256 identity for
each model. RNNoise source weights are BSD-3-Clause, DF3 relies on the
DeepFilterNet repository's MIT/Apache-2.0 grant, and Whisper tiny.en is MIT.

The serializer is invoked explicitly with the fetcher's Python interpreter.
It is installed as data without an executable shebang; its upstream source
and licence notice are preserved in the source package.
